1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'helvetica neue'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'times new roman'; color: #333333; background: #f9f7ee;"&gt;History of Sweetwater Valley, Tennesse
2 CONC e, pp. 283-285, by William Ballard Lenoir. 1919. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: roboto; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'times new roman'; color: #545454; background: white;"&gt;Richmond : Presbyterian C
2 CONC ommittee of Publication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman';"&gt;https://archive.org/details/historyofsweetwa00leno&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><li
2 CONC ne>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;WILLIAM RUTHERFORD&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Was born in Grayson County, Va., o
2 CONC n April 11, 1797, and came to Sweetwater Valley, first living near Reagan Station until 1864. During the remainder of the war he lived at the old Bowman (Benson) place. He died on June 25, 1870, and was buried at County Line Cemetery. He married Ce
2 CONC lia Hale, who was born in Grayson County, Va. She moved to Kaufman County, Texas,&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;in 1877, and died there and was buried at College Mound, Texas. Their children were:&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-indent: -.
