2 CONC d7;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, tahoma, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium; line-height: normal; background-color: #f6f5d7;"&gt;THE EWING GENEALOGY WITH COGNATE BRACHES: page 153:...Henry Filmer, son of Sir Edward Filmer, of Eas
2 CONC t Sutton, Kent, England, came to Virginia before 1642; was a Burgess for James City County 1642-1643, and soon after removed to Warwick County, where he was living as late as 1673. He married Elizabeth (surname not given) and had a daughter Martha
2 CONC , who married Thomas Green. They had a son Thomas Green (1665-1730), who married Elizabeth Marston (Nov. 25, 1672-Aug. 11, 1759), and had a son Thomas Marston Green, who was born in James City county, married Martha, daughter of Filmer Wills, and l
2 CONC ater removed to Miss. Thomas M. and Martha Green had a son Abner Gfeen, who was born Jan. 21, 1762, married Nov. 1, 1784, Mary, daughter of Colonel Anthony Hutchins...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
