2 TITL Richard Cradocke Will written 4 June 1618 Brightling, Sussex, England
1 _OID 3d495d2b-ef49-4cd3-9274-074838c16037
1 DATE 4 Jun 1618
1 PLAC Brightling, Sussex, England
1 _DSCR Probated in July. He died the 18th of June
2 CONT 
2 CONT The will mentions son in Law Thomas Vigor also Waight. (My 11th GGF) married to his daughter Mary and their sons James Vigor (line 30 and 31)  and Thomas, and daughter Constance  https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:S3HY-6MZ9-H4W?cat=685691
1 _META <metadataxml><transcription>First attempt at transcripton:
2 CONT  Thomas Craddock’s will
2 CONT 
2 CONT In the Name of God Amen. The fourteenth day of June in the year of our lord God, one 
2 CONT Thousand six hundred eighteen, I Richard Craddock of Brightling in the county of Sussex Kemmar being
2 CONT of good mynd &amp; in good &amp; perfect remembrance, thanks be to Almighty God do make and ordain this my last will 
2 CONT &amp; testament in manner and form following. That is to say first I bequeath my soul onto Almighty  God my
2 CONT Lord redeemer &amp; my body to be buried in the parish churchyard of Brightling aforesaid. Item I will onto the 
2 CONT poor of the parish of Brightling ?? shilling”s to be distributed at my burial at the discretion of my overseers
2 CONT of ? my last will &amp; testament. Item I will that all such debt &amp; duties as of right do owe to any person or
2 CONT person be all &amp; truly contented and paid by myne executors hereafter named without any delay or contradiction.
2 CONT Item I will and give unto Thomas my son five pounds of lawful money of England to be paid unto him within
2 CONT two years after my death and if I shall happen that Thomas my son doe dye before the expiration of the said
2 CONT Two year: then? My will is that the said five pounds be equally divided between John  Craddock &amp; Thomas 
2 CONT Craddock sons to the said Thomas Craddock or &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  to any one of them &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  shall ? be living. Item I give unto the said 
2 CONT John Craddock and Thomas Craddock to either of them five shillings to be paid unto them within one year after my
2 CONT death. Item I will &amp; give unto Constance Craddock the daughter of the said Thomas Cradock my son &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  shillings
2 CONT to be paid unto her within one year after my death. Item I will unto Sarah the wife of William Lukson my 
2 CONT daughter five pounds of lawful money of England to be paid unto the said Sarah within two year after
2 CONT my death and if It shall happen that the said Sarah my daughter di decease before expiration  of the said two
2 CONT years, them my will is that the said five pounds be equally divided among her children. Item I give onto ??
2 CONT Elizabeth the daughter of the said William Luksom &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; shillings to be paid unto her with ? years after
2 CONT My death. Item I will onto Liddia the wife of Thomas Sagett five pounds of lawful money of England to be paid
2 CONT Unto the said Liddia my daughter within two years after my decease and if it shall happen that the said Liddia
2 CONT My daughter doe decease before the expiration of the said two years, them my will is that the said five pounds, 
2 CONT Be equally divided among her children. Item I will unto Constance Sagett, Ann Sagett daughters of the 
2 CONT said Thomas Sagett &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; Shillings a pair to be paid onto either of them within one year after my death.
2 CONT Item I will onto Elizabeth the wife of Thomas Burgis my kinswoman &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;pou?&amp;rsqb;. Item I will onto James Reed,
2 CONT Richard Reed the sons of John Reed my kinsmen to either of them &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; pound. Item I will onto Constance
2 CONT Reed, Dorothia Reed, Mary Reed and Liddia Reed the daughters of the aforesaid John Reed my son in law &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;
2 CONT twentie shillings a pair to be paid onto each of them withing &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; years after my death. Item I will unto Mary 
2 CONT Jarratt, Sarah Jarratt, Elisabeth Jarratt the daughters of Thomas Jarratt my son in law &amp;lsqb;twenties&amp;rsqb; shillings
2 CONT a price to be paid onto either of them withing one year after my death. Item I will onto James Vigor and Thomas 
2 CONT Vigor the sons of Thomas Vigor also Waight my son in law, to either of them &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; pounds. Item I will
2 CONT unto Constance the daughter of the said Thomas Vigor also Waight twenties shillings to be paid onto her
2 CONT within two years after my death. Item I will onto Martha Woodsell the daughter of John Woodsell my son in 
2 CONT law five pounds of lawfull money of England to be payd onto the said Martha within  &amp;lsqb;three?&amp;rsqb; years after my death
2 CONT &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; to be putt out by my executor to the use and profit for the said Martha and my executor &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; to enter into of
2 CONT &amp;lsqb;sufficient&amp;rsqb; hand onto the overseer of this my will &amp; testament for the &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; performance thereof, &amp; if it shall happen that
2 CONT the said Martha does decease before &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; onto the age of eighteen year  and &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;   &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; marry:
2 CONT then my will is that Constance Woodsell &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;   &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; five pounds  &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  bequeath &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  profited
2 CONT &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;   &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;  &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; if any be. Item I will onto Constance Woodsell the daughter of the said John Woodsell &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;
2 CONT Twenty shillings to be payd onto her within one year after my death. Item I will onto Constance Read the
2 CONT daughter of Richard Reed my son in law, twenty shillings to be paid onto her within &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; years after
2 CONT my death. Item my will is that if any of my kinwomen before nominated onto whom I have given &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;
2 CONT aforesaid, so happen to decease before &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; appointed for the payment thereof be expired, then my
2 CONT will is that  ( &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;&amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;&amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; thereafter) I give portion ? equally divided between my other kinswomen &amp;lsqb;still&amp;rsqb; living
2 CONT onto &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; and &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; bequeath legacies as aforesaid (onto Martha Woodsell her portion  &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;), &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb;? I bequeath
2 CONT in full manor &amp; form as is aforsaid. ???? , my funeral expense. All ? lecacies, my will is be fulfilled and paid by my 
2 CONT executor in full manors and form as is aforesaid. ? my funeral expenses ?
2 CONT disregarded ? for approximately of ? my said will. ?? expanses? ??
2 CONT ? and my legacies being paid my is will is that it is equally divided between Ann the wife John Woodsell
2 CONT &amp; Constance the wife of Richard Read my daughters. Lastly, I do make John Woddsell &amp;lsqb;?&amp;rsqb; my son in laws my 
2 CONT Executor of this my last will &amp; testament. ? I do make ordeyne and appoint John ? , George ?man
2 CONT Toe be my overseer of this my last will and testament and I allow from ??? and labor herein ???
2 CONT To be paid from myne executor.</transcription></metadataxml>
