1 DATE 13 Jan 1693
1 PLAC Salem, Essex, Massachusetts
1 _DSCR Father Francis Faulkner and Uncle Joseph Marble put up bail for young sisters, Dorothy and Abigail Faulkner Jr. accused of witch craft.
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription>January 13, 169(2)3, Friday, Salem, Essex, Massachusetts; At least six more prisoners were temporarily released on bail pledged before Chief Justice William Stoughton. William Barker Jr. and his cousin Mary w
2 CONC ere freed on 100 pounds put up by her father, John Barker, and John Osgood. A like sum promised by Francis Faulkner and Joseph Marble freed the sisters Dorothy and Abigail Faulkner Jr. (whose mother was still under a death sentence.) </transcriptio
2 CONC n></metadataxml>
