2 TITL Hale Dougherty Bible pg 84
1 _OID ab421841-f72c-416b-a57a-33c7f45048c6
1 DATE 1810 - 1954
1 PLAC Virginia to Texas to California
1 _DSCR Story of the Hale Dougherty Bible
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT Important Note:
2 CONT All information on this page was graciously contributed by Bob Hillskemper  BobhillsJr@aol.com
2 CONT and can be found on the internet at http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.ancestry.com/chale/bible.html
2 CONT 
2 CONT I am making a rather awkward attempt to post this information to my family tree on ancestory.com which did not seem to allow for posting in html. Therefore I have broken the information provided so professionally by Bob Hills Jr. into jpeg files co
2 CONC ntaining images of the referenced Hale/Dougherty Bible pages and a cut and paste text edition of Mr. Hills' words describing the Hale Dougherty Bible. The important matter here is to share this information and document with any and all descendant
2 CONC s of the people whose lives are documented in this historical document.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT On 18 June 1839, Rosamond J. Hale, a daughter of Lewis Hale and Elizabeth Bourne, married Charles Dougherty in Grayson County, Virginia.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Thus was started the Dougherty Family Bible into which was recorded the birth, marriage and death data for the entire family. Likewise, the same data was recorded for the entire Lewis Hale family.
2 CONT 
2 CONT The bible has survived over the generations, including the journey the Dougherty family made when they moved from Elk Creek, Virginia to Texas in 1851 and then on to Southern California by Covered Wagon Train in 1868.
2 CONT 
2 CONT The Family Record pages of the bible are reproduced below. A typed up summary of the personal data in the bible is also provided to assist the reader to read the original text. Supplementary information has been added in the summary to supply addit
2 CONC ional details. Since this supplementary information is not a part of the original bible text, it appears within brackets [ ].
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription>Births [Pg. 84]
2 CONT 
2 CONT George W. Hale - Sept. 7, 1810 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Rufus M. Hale - Mar. 15, 1815 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Andrew J. Hale - July 18, 1816 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Samuel [Hale] - June 17, 1817 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Elvira B. Hale - Feb. 18, 1820 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Rosamond J. Hale - Feb. 12, 1822 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Lewis F. Hale - Feb. 23, 1824 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Peyton G. Hale - Nov. 27, 1825 - [see note 1]
2 CONT Franklin Hale - Jan. 11, 1807
2 CONT Stephen M. Hale - Feb. 12, 1813
2 CONT Crockett J. H. Davenport - Sept. 14, 1838 - [see note 3]
2 CONT James L. Davenport - Mar. 19, 1840 - [see note 3
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT Deaths [Pg. 84]
2 CONT 
2 CONT Mary Luvenia Preston - July 17, 1932 - [nee, Dougherty]
2 CONT William J. Dougherty - [no date]
2 CONT Martha J. Dougherty King - [no date]
2 CONT Nancy P. Dougherty Price - [no date]
2 CONT John L. Dougherty - [no date]
2 CONT James L. Dougherty - [no date]
2 CONT Margaret Virginia Knott - Jan. 14, 1954 - [nee, Dougherty, d. Garden Grove, Los Angeles Co., CA]
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT </transcription></metadataxml>
