2 TITL jameshenrybeggsandfamily
1 _OID bf594051-a449-4d53-bdbe-974c9dd75be1
1 DATE circa 1910
1 PLAC Hunt County Texas
1 _DSCR James Henry and Julia Ann Smith Beggs Family 
2 CONT 
2 CONT This photo and the following story was found on HuntGenweb.com where it was posted from a Beggs newsletter prepared by Ruby Beggs Davis.  It mentions an interaction with Jack Hale.  Thus I took the liberty of posting it here.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT This photo is of my great grandfather and great grandmother, James Henry and Julia Ann Smith Beggs and their children. They were married on the 20th of September 1868. They went to Hunt County Texas and settled at Shady Grove, Texas. They establish
2 CONC ed a home on Mr. Jack Hale's place and had several years crops. They then moved to Campbell, Texas Hunt Co.and acquired 128 1/2 acres and lived there until they died. They had nine children in all. The first child was a baby girl, who died as a ba
2 CONC y and is buried at Shiloh Community Cemetery.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Front Row: John Benjamin Beggs b. 17 Oct. 1896 d.25 Jan. 1929 m. Prude Sweat 1909
2 CONT James Henry Beggs seated and Julia Ann Smith Beggs seated.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Back Row Leslie Eugene Beggs b. 19 July 1883 d. 12 Apr. 1909 m. Carrie B. Clemons
2 CONT James Milton Beggs b. 7 Feb. 1874 d. 21 Dec. 1947 m. Mary Duncan 1903
2 CONT Irving Holman Beggs b. 11 Nov. 1889 d. 17 Sept. 1931 m. Ala Chapman 1917
2 CONT Albert Alonzo Beggs b. 1 Apr.1880 d 30 Sept. 1961 m. Susan Pippin 1899
2 CONT Lula Magnolia Beggs b. 21 Dec.1876 d.1943 m. Willie Austin Pollard 1899
2 CONT Thomas Henry Beggs b. 6 June 1887 d.16 Oct. 1980 m. Mrs. Otha R. England
2 CONT Irene Lee Beggs b. 16 Dec. 1892 d. 13 Dec. 1920 m. Charlie Gilmore
2 CONT Not pictured is Martha Ann Beggs b. 22 Mar. 1871 d. 28 Aug.1876
2 CONT 
2 CONT When James and Julia were married, James had one horse, saddle and bridle and Julia had a few housekeeping things. They had no money or property. The home that the family lived in had 3 rooms 16 foot square. There was a big fireplace in the livin
2 CONC g room. The kitchen was in the back with a long eating table and a big cook stove. They had a gasoline engine pump that pumped water to over head tank. Water was piped in, a big feature in that day and time. They had a milk house and smoke house. T
2 CONC hey had 3 or 4 milk cows and an orchard of peaches, pears and apples. There was about 1/4 acre garden, where they grew what they needed. They took their grain to Wolfe City where they had it grounded.
2 CONT 
2 CONT The above was from a Beggs newsletter prepared by Ruby Beggs Davis. Ruby is a descendant of James Henry and his first wife Elizabeth Beets.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Submitted by: Leslie Leon Beggs, grandson of John Benjamin. 
