2 TITL Story of the Hale Dougherty Bible
1 _OID eb8653d8-fdbb-49e7-9f4a-dc09c1fe9cae
1 DATE 1839 to 1954
1 PLAC From  Virginia to Texas and on to California
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;font size="1"&gt;Preface:&lt;br&gt;All information on this page was graciously contributed/posted on the internet by Bob Hillskemper&amp;nbsp; BobhillsJr@@aol.com&lt;br&gt;and can be found on the i
2 CONC nternet using the weblink at the bottom of the Andrew Jackson Hale profile page in this fmily tree. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;font size="1"&gt;I am making a rather awkward attempt to post this information to my famil
2 CONC y tree on ancestory.com which did not seem to allow for posting in html. Therefore I have broken the information provided so professionally by Bob Hills Jr. into jpeg files containing images of the referenced Hale/Dougherty Bible pages and a cut an
2 CONC d paste text edition of Mr. Hills&amp;#39; words describing the Hale Dougherty Bible. The important matter here is to share this information and document with any and all descendants of the people whose lives are documented in this historical docum
2 CONC ent.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;See the accompanying jpeg images of the Bible pages&amp;nbsp; 81, 82, 83, 84 also posted here. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div align="center"&gt;&lt;strong&g
2 CONC t;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Story of the Hale Dougherty Bible&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;On 18 June 1839, Rosamond J. Hale, a daughter of Lewis Hale and Elizabeth Bourne, married Charles Dougherty in Gr
2 CONC ayson County, Virginia.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Thus was started the Dougherty Family Bible into which was recorded the birth, marriage and death data for the entire family. Likewise, the same data was recorded for the entire Lewis Hale family.&lt;br&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;br&gt;The bible has survived over the generations, including the journey the Dougherty family made when they moved from Elk Creek, Virginia to Texas in 1851 and then on to Southern California by Covered Wagon Train in 1868.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
2 CONC The Family Record pages of the bible are reproduced below. A typed up summary of the personal data in the bible is also provided to assist the reader to read the original text. Supplementary information has been added in the summary to supply addit
2 CONC ional details. Since this supplementary information is not a part of the original bible text, it appears within brackets [ ].&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notes:&lt;br&gt;1 - Child of Lewis Hale Jr. and Elizabeth Bourne.&lt;br&gt;2 - Child of Charl
2 CONC es Dougherty and Rosamond J. Hale.&lt;br&gt;3 - Son of J. B. Davenport and Elvira B. Hale, adopted by Lewis Hale and Elizabeth Hale (nee Bourne) after the death of Elvira Davenport, nee Hale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Births [Bible Pg. 81]&lt;br
2 CONC &gt;&lt;br&gt;Charles Dougherty - Dec. 27, 1805 - [Guilford Co., NC]&lt;br&gt;Rosamond J. Dougherty - Feb. 12, 1822 - [nee Hale, see note 1]&lt;br&gt;Martha J. Dougherty - Apr. 24, 1840 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;William J. Dougherty - May 29, 184
2 CONC 1 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;Mary L. Dougherty - Oct. 4, 1842 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;John L. Dougherty - Apr. 12, 1844 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;Elvira E. Dougherty - Oct. 14, 1845 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;James L. Dougherty - June 17, 1847 - [see not
2 CONC e 2]&lt;br&gt;Nancy P. Dougherty - Dec. 17, 1848 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;Sarah T. Dougherty - June 17, 1850 - [see note 2]&lt;br&gt;Charles Middlet[on] Dougherty - Dec. 10, 1857 - [see note 2, stillborn]&lt;br&gt;Carrie M. W. Dougherty - Aug. 12, 1
2 CONC 860 - [see note 2, adopted]&lt;br&gt;Margaret Virginia Dougherty - Feb. 19, 1866 - [see note 2, b. Hunt Co. Texas]&lt;br&gt;Lewis Hale - May 14, 1781 - [Lewis, Jr.]&lt;br&gt;Elizabeth Hale - Mar. 20, 1785 - [nee, Bourne]&lt;br&gt;Celia Hale - Dec
2 CONC . 18, 1805 - [see note 1]&lt;br&gt;Permelia Hale - Feb. 1, 1806 - [see note 1]&lt;br&gt;Cynthia G. Hale - June 1, 1808 - [see note 1]&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Marriages [Bible Pg. 82]&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Charles Dougherty an
2 CONC d Tobitha Winchester - Nov. 23, 1837 - [Tobitha and first child died in childbirth]&lt;br&gt;Charles Dougherty and Rosamond J. Hale - June 18, 1839&lt;br&gt;Martha J. Dougherty and John C. King - Oct. 20, 1858&lt;br&gt;James Preston and Mary L. Dou
2 CONC gherty - Nov. 17, 1864&lt;br&gt;John L. Dougherty and H. [?] O&amp;#39;Landon - Dec. 6, 1864&lt;br&gt;E. C. Knott and Maggie V. Dougherty - June 9, 1887 - [Margaret Virginia Dougherty]&lt;br&gt;James L. Dougherty and Callie Barling - Mar., 1868&lt;
2 CONC br&gt;J. D. Price and Nannie P. Dougherty - May 21, 1871 - [ Nancy P.]&lt;br&gt;Lewis Hale and Elizabeth Bourn - Feb. 11, 1801&lt;br&gt;Elvira B. Hale and J. B. Davenport - Nov. 28, 1837&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deaths [Bibl
2 CONC e Pg. 83]&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tobitha Dougherty, Consort of Charles Dougherty, - Aug. 7, 1838 - [died in childbirth, see marriage above]&lt;br&gt;Elvira E. Dougherty - Nov. 11, 1851 - [buried along side the trail, near Little Rock, AR]&lt;
2 CONC br&gt;Sarah T. Dougherty - Dec. 14, 1851 - [died Hunt County, TX]&lt;br&gt;Charles Middleton [Dougherty] - Dec. 10, 1857 - [stillborn]&lt;br&gt;Carrie M. W. Dougherty, adopted daughter of Charles and Rosamond Dougherty - Jan. 29, 1864 - [died, Hun
2 CONC t County, TX]&lt;br&gt;Rosamond J. Dougherty - Dec. 19, 1912 - [nee Hale, died Azusa, L.A. Co., CA]&lt;br&gt;Charles Dougherty - Nov. 13, 1879 - [Died, Azusa, L.A. Co., CA]&lt;br&gt;Lewis F. Hale - Sept. 28, 1824 - [see note 1]&lt;br&gt;Elvira Dave
